WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.980
Let's go beyond the legendary Fortnite skins.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.640
Here are some of the rarest Fortnite skins
around.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.740
The Reaper

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:11.610
The Reaper is the crown jewel of Season 3's
Hired Gun set, which just so happened to resemble

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:16.700
Keanu Reeves' character, John Wick, the infamous
assassin with a soft spot for puppies.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.380
The Season 3 Battle Pass Announcement came
complete with The Reaper skin jumping from

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.440
an explosion, machine gun in hand.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.120
"Yeah.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.360
I'm thinkin' I'm back!"

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.960
Recon Expert

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.760
When Battle Royale debuted, players didn't
appreciate all the skins that were available.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.280
One such example from season 1 is possibly
the rarest in the game: the Recon Expert.

00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:40.559
Outwardly, she's not too interesting, and
didn't seem worth the initial 1,200 V-Bucks

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.080
cost.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.360
But her rarity is directly connected to the
lackluster look, since no one bought the skin

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.480
before it disappeared from the shop.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.760
Aerial Assault Trooper

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.219
Another Season 1 throwback, the Aerial Assault
Trooper was one of the first skins available

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:57.300
in Battle Royale, so only players who first
joined the game's hype train had access to

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:57.820
it.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.580
Again, players missed out on the Aerial Assault
Trooper because of its lack of flash.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.400
Despite not being one of the most exciting
skins, this one definitely has the power of

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.380
nostalgia behind it.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.200
Renegade Raider

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.260
Renegade Raider is also from Fortnite's first
season, but this one has a little moxie.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.220
After achieving Level 20, players could purchase
this outfit in the seasonal shop and were

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.880
probably drawn to her post-apocalyptic look.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.460
Just as the Reaper resembles John Wick, Renegade
Raider recalls another movie character: Tank

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.000
Girl.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.520
Keep your eye out if Epic decides to make
this available for late-comers to add to their

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.440
wardrobes.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.480
Merry Marauder

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.060
Merry Marauder and his frowny-faced gingerbread
mask came with the Merry Christmas set.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.620
These skins were only available for a limited
time, and while the Merry Marauder didn't

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.290
have the same fanatic following that the Halloween
skins did, if you didn't grab them at the

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.060
time, you'll never get to wear them — unless
Epic brings them back in the future to spread

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:49.900
some Christmas fear.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.820
Black Knight

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.080
The Black Knight is the glowing-eyed scourge
of the Wailing Woods that was released as

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.960
a part of the Fort Knights set back in Season
2.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.740
A just reward for those who achieved max level,
players covet it for the reputation points

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:04.440
it signifies.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.960
And despite the Red Knight's later availability
in the shop, those who worked hard to get

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.880
the Black Knight skin still remain the only
players who've earned the exclusive right

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.660
to wear the armor of the darkest of the Fort
Knights.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.220
The Galaxy

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:22.080
Galaxy is probably the most literally expensive
Fortnite skin, exclusive to owners of the

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.100
$650 Samsung Galaxy Tab S4, or the $1,000
Galaxy Note 9 phone.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.170
The Galaxy skin was announced ahead of the
Fortnite Android Beta and quickly became a

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.160
fan-fave.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.520
Ragnarok Skin

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:39.080
If you really want to be the Vi-king of Fortnite...you'll
probably have found some way to get the Ragnarok

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.300
skin during season 5.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.400
Only available to players skilled enough to
kill their way up to Tier 100 that season,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.460
Ragnarok is the mark of a dedicated player
and testament to how Epic Games' likes to

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.600
treat its best and most brutal Battle Royale
players.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.620
Suffice it to say...it ragna-rocks.

